 # JSON utility
 
-Run `python cli.py` with JSON on stdin. The identity action returns its value unchanged.
+Run `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin; one JSON result is printed on stdout.
+
+## Actions
+
+- `identity`: returns `payload["value"]` unchanged, for any JSON value.
+- `distance` (also accepted as `action_distance`): expects `grid` (rectangular list of strings of `.` and `#`, dimensions 1..30), `start` and `end` as `[row, column]` integer coordinates inside the grid. Returns the shortest orthogonal path length (edge count) avoiding `#`, or `null` when unreachable. A blocked `start` or `end` returns `null`, even when `start` and `end` are the same blocked cell. Same open cell returns `0`.
+
+## Example
+
+    echo '{"action":"distance","grid":["...",".#.","..."],"start":[0,0],"end":[2,2]}' | python cli.py
+    # => 4
+
+## Errors and boundaries
+
+Unknown actions raise `ValueError`; the CLI exits with code 2, prints the error message to stderr (no traceback), and stdout stays empty. Invalid JSON input behaves the same way. Operations never mutate the input payload, including on failure. Types, shapes and bounds are guaranteed by contract except for the specified validation errors.
